{
  "_about": [
    "The app's information architecture, in one file. src/ui/shell.js renders the rail and the phase bar from this and nothing else, so adding a module is a JSON edit. `status` is honest on purpose: 'built' links somewhere real, 'partial' links to the step that half-covers it today, 'planned' renders a stub that says what it will do. Never let a module claim 'built' before it is.",
    "PHASE `hue` MUST EQUAL PHASE `id`. Two emitters build the colour class from the hue — launcher.js `sh-ph-${phase.hue}` and shell.js, twice — while palette.js builds it from the id. They only ever agreed because the original six phases had hue === id. Setting hue to a colour name during the four-pillar restructure made the hub emit .sh-ph-feature and .sh-ph-shorts, which match no rule in tokens.css, so --hue was undefined and those phases rendered in currentColor — the silent failure CLAUDE.md records the breakdown shipping for two commits. tokens.css maps the ID to a colour; this field must not disagree with it."
  ],
